[Music]  one of the reasons that the stock market  has been on such a tear over the past  five years or so is that debt has been  relatively cheap  people have been able to go to the bank  borrow money and invest that in the  stock market with the promise that the  stock market would generate higher  returns the problem is that inflation  has encouraged central banks to increase  interest rates in the hope of reducing  prices we can see here the effect that  has had on debt here in the middle of  2020 the yields or the interest provided  by u.s bonds  was near half a percent in the space of  just a month or two that has jumped to  three percent that means it's harder to  borrow money and spend it on the stock  market we can see the effect that that  has had on stocks particularly meme  stocks these companies that had a really  good lock down from an investment  perspective have lost in some instances  three quarters their value in the space  of just three months the likes of  kavanagh roblox and coinbase the point  of comparison according to the bloomberg  opinion columnist john authors is the  tech bubble of the year 2000.  back then the difference in valuation  between tech stocks and  the rest of the market had broadened and  spread in the year 2021 and 2022 the  difference between tech stocks and the  rest of the market was at a similar  level there has been a bit of a  correction but if the lessons of the  millennium met anything to go by there  may still be some way to go

